# Shell scripts are LF, whatever the checkout platform.
#
# A shell script with CRLF endings is not a slightly-odd file: it does not run.
# bash reads the carriage return as part of each command, so the shebang line
# fails with `$'\r': command not found` and `set -o pipefail` becomes an
# invalid option name. Git Bash tolerates it; WSL bash, and every Linux and
# macOS host, do not.
#
# This repo develops on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise
# hand a tracked .sh file CRLF endings on checkout and break it for everyone
# who is not on Git Bash.
#
# It cost a dead wizard to learn (2026-09-23), though that one was generated
# into gitignored .scratch/ and so was never git's to normalise. This rule
# covers the tracked case: a wizard promoted to scripts/ as a repeatable setup
# path, a CI helper, a hook.
*.sh text eol=lf
